# Wave W17-T (Route 134): gate rock — gate rock at the falls\u2019 foot standing in the lane\u2019s water: a pale, spray-wet shore rock — the falls\u2019 mist keeps its crown bright, spray flecks standing on its upper faces, the gate stone of the delivery channel; foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it (design: Perennial\u2019s falls pouring east into white water at the foot — the town-side frame byte-preserved; the rock kind carries the falls\u2019 register only). Route 134\u2019s own rock — the fleet\u2019s palest, wettest lane rock: split from Route 133\u2019s dark long-jointed rapid rock by value entire, and from Route 126\u2019s massive-jointed crater rock by finish (spray-wet gate stone vs dry crater wall).
